# The liveness job's timer (SPEC-027, SPEC-032; ADR-027): every hour, at minute 14, the dead-man
# watch and the drift check. The job table in crates/coordination/src/jobs.rs is the one schedule,
# and crates/coordination/tests/job_table.rs holds this calendar equal to it. The calendar is written
# in UTC, the neutral zone; the private rail renders the deployment's own zone (deploy/README.md).
# With no Unit=, the timer starts the job instance of its own name.
[Unit]
Description=DeckStreak's hourly liveness watch, at minute 14
X-DurableServices-Waive=calendar-not-persistent the job table makes the watch no catch-up job (ADR-027): it runs every hour, so the next check replaces one missed while the host was down
X-DurableServices-Waive=randomized-delay-missing the job table places each job on its own minute (ADR-027), and a random delay would move each fire off its minute

[Timer]
OnCalendar=*-*-* *:14:00 UTC

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
